From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Implement getentropy with ADC noise and ChaCha20

Collect 1024 microphone ADC samples through the ARM7 microphone service,
reject busy, missing, stuck, strongly biased or trivially alternating
input, and condition it with SHA-256 alongside timing and input data.
Use ChaCha20 with per-request key rotation and reseed after 1 MiB.

Preserve microphone capture settings and amplifier state. Bound sampling
waits and fail with EIO without touching the output on required seed
failure. Keep the POSIX 256-byte limit and never fall back to a clock seed.

This remains experimental: the ADC entropy rate has not been measured
on hardware, and the health checks do not establish cryptographic security.
---
